# mlir_gen_bug.ledger — programs that TRIP THE R2 SELF-DIAGNOSIS CHANNEL and
# are excluded from its hard failure BY NAME.
#
# R2: a message mlir-gen emits ABOUT ITSELF ("statement DROPPED", "unknown
# tagged enum") must make the compile FAIL. Before that rule, mlir-gen printed
# such a line, wrote the object file and returned 0 — so a test could pass while
# a WRITE had silently vanished. Turning the rule on made these programs red:
# each was ALREADY being miscompiled and passing. None of them is a separator
# defect; each has its cause in another phase and its own arc.
#
# Format:  <test-base> <count> <path relative to the repo root, no .logos>
# `count` is the number of `mlir_gen: internal:` lines the program emits.
# Held in BOTH directions by logos_00_mlir_gen_bug_ledger: a program that stops
# tripping, trips fewer times, or trips more times is RED. A fixed defect must
# DELETE its row here — THIS FILE IS THE ONLY PLACE THE EXCLUDED SET IS NAMED.
# (This line used to say "and from MLIRGEN_BUG_LEDGER in
# tests/logos/CMakeLists.txt". That list is gone: the population is derived from
# this artifact and every test is handed the ledger's PATH unconditionally, so
# logosc asks whether the program it is compiling is listed. The sentence was
# the last surviving reference to the second copy whose drift caused `pat_6` to
# be red on the full suite while its ledger row was green — i.e. this line was
# itself an instance of the defect the CMake comment records.)
#
# ── the cause, per entry ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# issue-41888-b170 / nested-tuple-in-variant-payload-b170
#   `unknown tagged enum '<name>__<args>'` — mono never emitted the demanded
#   generic-enum instance (the args include `<error>` residue, i.e. a type that
#   never resolved). A MONO instantiation defect, not a naming one.
# res-and-or-comb-or
#   the same, plus the `let` that consumed the missing instance being dropped.
#   `Result__i32__F` — `F` is an unsubstituted fn-type param.
# pat_6
#   `let ai` / `let bi` produced no value: a struct pattern over a GENERIC
#   struct (`GPair<u8,u16>`) binds fields whose initialisers lower to nothing,
#   so the bound names are unbound and every dependent statement vanishes.
#   A generic struct-pattern binding arc, not a naming one.
# intrinsic_2
#   `unsupported cast: no lowering from 'i32' to '!llvm.array<0 x Type>'` at
#   line 95: `if args_of::<Plain>() != [] as [Type; 0] { return 28; }`. An EMPTY
#   ARRAY LITERAL has no element type — sema says so out loud one line earlier
#   ("warning: empty array literal: element type unknown") and lowers it as a
#   placeholder i32, which no cast can turn into a zero-length aggregate. So the
#   comparison lowered to nothing and the `@rule intrinsic.reflect.args-of`
#   assertion "non-generic => empty" HAS NEVER BEEN EVALUATED, on any compiler,
#   since it was written. An EMPTY-ARRAY-LITERAL TYPING arc (the element type
#   must come from the cast/annotation before mlir-gen, not from a cast after
#   it), not a cast-lowering one — teaching `coerce_to` to answer here would be
#   inventing a value for an expression sema declined to type.
#
#   ⚠ THIS ROW IS NOT A REGRESSION AND NOT A NEW DEFECT. It is the R2 channel
#   finally SEEING a miscompile that has always been there: the raw `fprintf` at
#   the unsupported-cast site never reached the exit code, so the program
#   compiled, ran, and passed with the assertion silently absent. Routing that
#   site through `bug_null` is what made it visible, exactly as turning the rule
#   on originally made seven others visible. The generated object is byte-for-
#   byte what it was — this row restores the STATUS QUO of the artifact while
#   putting the defect under re-measurement.
#
# ── CLOSED SINCE, rows DELETED (each now compiles clean and RUNS correctly) ──
# empty-struct-braces-b151  — `E::Empty4 {}` is a BRACE-EMPTY variant: no
#   payload, so the enum is plain C-style and has no tagged representation to
#   resolve. The syntax said "data variant"; the payload is the fact.
#   Fixed in mlir_gen_expr.cpp (gen_expr_kind(EEnumLitDataView)).
# core_1_adv_unit_field     — a ZERO-WIDTH struct field (`u: ()`) has no slot,
#   so `gep_field` could not name one and the whole struct literal lowered to
#   nothing. Nothing to store is not a failure. Fixed in mlir_gen.cpp
#   (gen_struct_lit); the initialiser is still evaluated for its effects.
# irrefutable-unit-b142     — the `let` canary excluded value-less types by a
#   KIND LIST (Void, Never). `()` is a zero-arity Tuple and an empty struct is
#   a Struct — both zero-width. The predicate is now the structural one its
#   sibling guard already used (`logos_to_mlir(ty)` non-null).
issue-41888-b170                     1 tests/imported/pass/match/issue-41888-b170
nested-tuple-in-variant-payload-b170 1 tests/imported/pass/match/nested-tuple-in-variant-payload-b170
res-and-or-comb-or                   4 tests/imported/pass/option-result/res-and-or-comb-or
pat_6                                4 tests/spec/pass/pat_6
intrinsic_2                          1 tests/spec/pass/intrinsic_2
